w  well it's been handled so far given the  incredibly difficult task that the  series set itself by starting at the  pinnacle of power and knowledge it is  very difficult to go on a journey when  you've already attained everything and  other series that start at the more  level one beginning a much more easily  forgiven in the early days we're not  going crazy with their focus because the  protagonist is usually weak and ignorant  a combination that really favors slow  world building what I'll also say for  overlord is that I do enjoy the comedy  for the most part in fact probably one  of my favorite moments in the series  thus far is that random scene in my  mangas bedroom where Demio caches are  better and just casually asks is that a  lord  inés body-pillow and not only that but  they both just moved on as if this was a  fairly innocuous occurrence moments like  that are fantastic and with Alberto in  particular I also do like the  examination of what happens when you  force someone to love you because that  never works out in media and her  obsession with my manga is  simultaneously hilarious and quite  disturbing if I was to continue the  series my hope would be that this does  get expanded upon though and she doesn't  simply become a one-note I love Lord  ions character everytime she pops up  like maybe at one stage she is driven so  mad by love the chick commits a terrible  action it makes me wanna go oh [ __ ] this  is a serious problem but I'm not sure if  I'm putting too much of an expectation  on overload and here's the thing at the  moment I'm not really sure what overlord  is it appears to have a linear story but  it's progressing slowly and weirdly  giving focus to aspects of the world  that I quite honestly could not care  less about I mean there is a notion of  political intrigue in the background for  the various different factions but at  this stage that hasn't been expanded  upon enough to keep my interest it  definitely has some potential especially  since my manga seems to have a sharp  diplomatic mine  so maybe I just haven't placed enough  trust in overlord to continue it further  to where that becomes a selling factor  but it's difficult I think that Overlord  has had a pretty mess start and without  going into spoilers I'd love to know if  any of you have seen it to think it's  worth the investment to continue one  last thing if this first impressions  wasn't negative enough I also have to  say that I have a huge distaste for the  opening and ending of season 1 although  I will say that I enjoy the opening  infinitely more than the ending at least  it has a catchy chorus the ending though  to my ears is just noise an assortment  of random guitar riffs and extremely  distorted vocals and it doesn't do it  for me but yeah I'm going to put it to  you the comments section to see whether  or not I should continue the series so  please do let me in on your own personal  experiences with overlord and by all  means feel free to change my mind in the  least spoilery way possible but that  pretty much does it for my first  impressions of overlord if you enjoyed  this video and the content this channel  produce in general then please do  consider donating to the new world  review patreon because the support of  all of you amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share or subscribe because it also helps  plot this channel an incredible amount  and if you'd like to join the fun at any  time then please do head over to my  discord server where a wide array of  shenanigan ray takes place on a daily  basis and finally please do comment with  your thoughts on Overlord this has been  the new world review and I'll see you  next time  you

